// © MMT — Expansion Breakout v2 (MNQ 5m)
//
// WHAT THIS IS
// A long-only Donchian breakout taken when price is extended from the day's
// VWAP, outside yesterday's range, and above its ~50-day trend — during the
// New York morning only. The entry family came from an exhaustive sweep of
// 220,699,136 complete strategies over 7.6 years of 5-minute Nasdaq-100 data.
// The session window, the trend filter and the exits come from a second,
// deliberately small study of pre-registered hypotheses (backtest/improve.py),
// because the big sweep searched neither session nor trade management.
//
// Headline, measured one position at a time with costs charged, on 519,046
// bars from 2019-01-02 to 2026-08-10:
//
//     PF 1.45 at a 43.8% win rate, 129 trades/year, +247.5R, 15.2R drawdown
//
// against PF 1.18 / 48.3% / 319 per year for v1. Three other presets trade that
// mix differently — see the table further down.
//
// THE NUMBER THAT MATTERS MOST
// Excess over random entries drawn from bars that ALREADY pass every gate
// except the breakout itself is t = +4.63, against a selection-corrected bar of
// t = 3.82 for this study's ~1,500 tested cells. v1 scored t = +2.82 and did not
// clear its bar. This is the first configuration in the project that does.
// It is still one instrument, one regime-rich decade, and a 3.2x overlap
// correction away from a promise.
//
// WHAT CHANGED FROM v1 — three of these were bugs, not preferences
//   1. VWAP is now anchored to the ET CALENDAR DAY, computed here rather than
//      taken from ta.vwap(). Pine's built-in anchors to the exchange session,
//      which for CME index futures opens at 18:00 ET the previous day. Measured
//      against the research convention the two disagree by a MEDIAN of 1.34 ATR,
//      and on 85% of bars by more than 0.25 ATR. The entry gate is
//      |close - VWAP| >= 1.5 ATR, so v1 on a live chart was firing a materially
//      different signal set than the one that was validated.
//   2. Prior-day high/low is likewise accumulated on ET calendar days instead of
//      request.security(..., "D", ...), whose daily bar also runs 18:00-17:00 ET.
//      The "outside prior-day range" gate disagreed on 22.3% of bars.
//   3. Costs are charged by SESSION — 1.00 index point round turn in RTH, 1.75
//      overnight, matching the research. v1 charged the RTH number around the
//      clock, which quietly flattered every overnight trade.
//   4. Added: session gating, breakeven stop, ATR trailing stop, optional
//      flat-by-the-close, and a drawing lifecycle that does not leak line
//      objects.
//
// HOW TO READ THE DASHBOARD
// It grades every historical signal on YOUR data with costs charged and only
// one position held at a time, so you can verify the claims rather than trust
// them. Numbers are R-multiples: 1R is the initial stop distance.
//
// HONEST EXPECTATIONS — read before trading it
//   * See the dashboard's "Study expectation" row. Anything far above it on
//     your chart is a smaller sample, not a better strategy.
//   * Trades overlap ~3.2x if you let them. Every number here is measured one
//     position at a time, which is the only version an account can hold and is
//     under a third of the trade count a naive backtest reports.
//   * The short mirror still LOSES (PF 1.00 over the full sample, t = +1.12
//     against matched conditions) even with the trend filter inverted. Part of
//     what the long side earns is exposure to an index that rose 365%.
//   * 2025 was a flat year for it: PF 1.00, −0.1R across 140 trades. 2022, the
//     bear year that nearly broke v1, came in at PF 1.55 — the 50-day trend
//     filter is what bought that.
//   * Every preset trades the New York morning except "Max trades". Overnight
//     breakouts were the worst slice in the study (PF 0.97 out-of-sample) and
//     cost 75% more to trade.
//
//@version=6
// max_bars_back is set explicitly because ta.percentrank() reaches back as far
// as the ATR-percentile lookback input allows (up to 2000 bars). Left to
// auto-detection Pine sizes the buffer from the first bars it sees and then
// throws "the requested historical offset is beyond the buffer" deep into the
// history of a long chart.
indicator("MMT — Expansion Breakout v2 (MNQ 5m)", shorttitle="MMT ExpBrk2",
     overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500,
     max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 2500)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G_SET = "Setup"
preset = input.string("Balanced", "Preset", options =
     ["Balanced", "Max profit factor", "Max win rate", "Max trades", "Custom"],
     group = G_SET,
     tooltip = "Presets are measured rows from the study, all one-position-at-" +
     "a-time with costs charged. Custom exposes every value below.")

G_ENT = "Entry gates"
lookbackIn = input.int(12, "Breakout lookback (bars)", minval = 3, maxval = 200,
     group = G_ENT, tooltip = "Close must exceed the highest high of the prior " +
     "N bars. Results were stable across 12/24/48/96.")
volRankLen = input.int(500, "ATR percentile lookback", minval = 50, maxval = 2000,
     group = G_ENT)
volRankMinIn = input.float(0, "ATR percentile above", minval = 0, maxval = 100,
     group = G_ENT, tooltip = "0 disables, which is what every preset uses: " +
     "once entries are confined to the morning and to bars above the 50-day " +
     "trend, this gate stops adding anything (0.00 to 0.66 all score PF " +
     "1.65-1.67). Above 0.80 it clearly hurts.")
vwapMinIn = input.float(1.5, "Min |close - VWAP| in ATR", minval = 0, step = 0.1,
     group = G_ENT)
usePdIn = input.bool(true, "Require outside prior-day range", group = G_ENT,
     tooltip = "Price beyond yesterday's high or low — an actual expansion day " +
     "rather than rotation inside a known range.")
closePosMinIn = input.float(0.0, "Min close position in bar range", minval = 0,
     maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = G_ENT,
     tooltip = "0 disables. 0.7 means the breakout bar must close in the top " +
     "30% of its own range.")
relVolMinIn = input.float(0.0, "Min relative volume", minval = 0, step = 0.1,
     group = G_ENT, tooltip = "0 disables. Volume vs its own 20-bar average.")
marginAtrIn = input.float(0.0, "Clear the level by (x ATR)", minval = 0, step = 0.05,
     group = G_ENT, tooltip = "0 means a one-tick break counts.")
regimeIn = input.string("Above EMA3900", "Higher-horizon trend filter", options =
     ["None", "Above prior-day close", "Above EMA200", "Above EMA780",
      "Above EMA1560", "Above EMA3900"], group = G_ENT,
     tooltip = "On a 5-minute chart 780/1560/3900 bars are roughly 10, 20 and " +
     "50 trading days.")

G_SESS = "Session"
sessIn = input.string("RTH morning", "Trading window", options =
     ["All hours", "RTH 09:30-16:00", "RTH minus last 30m", "RTH morning",
      "07:00-16:00", "03:00-16:00"], group = G_SESS,
     tooltip = "An MNQ round turn costs ~1.00 index point in RTH and ~1.75 " +
     "overnight against a median 5m ATR near 11 points, so the session a trade " +
     "is taken in is a first-order effect, not a detail.")
useFlatIn = input.bool(false, "Force flat before the close", group = G_SESS)
flatByIn = input.int(960, "Flat by (ET minutes past midnight)", minval = 1,
     maxval = 1439, group = G_SESS, tooltip = "960 = 16:00 ET. A position is " +
     "closed on the bar that ENDS at this time, and no new position is opened " +
     "on that bar.")

G_EXIT = "Risk & exits"
stopAtrIn = input.float(2.0, "Stop (x ATR)", minval = 0.2, step = 0.1, group = G_EXIT)
rrIn = input.float(3.0, "Target (x risk)", minval = 0.2, step = 0.05, group = G_EXIT)
beIn = input.float(0.0, "Move stop to breakeven at (R)", minval = 0, step = 0.05,
     group = G_EXIT, tooltip = "0 disables. Converts losers into scratches: " +
     "profit factor up, win rate down.")
trailIn = input.float(0.0, "ATR trailing stop (x ATR at entry)", minval = 0,
     step = 0.1, group = G_EXIT, tooltip = "0 disables. Trails from the bar " +
     "CLOSE using the ATR measured at entry, so the distance never changes " +
     "mid-trade.")
maxHoldIn = input.int(48, "Time stop (bars)", minval = 5, group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "On a 5-minute chart 48 bars = 4 hours, 72 = 6h, 144 = 12h.")
atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = G_EXIT)

G_COST = "Costs"
costRth = input.float(1.00, "Round-turn cost, RTH (index points)", minval = 0,
     step = 0.25, group = G_COST, tooltip = "MNQ: ~$0.50/side commission + ~1 " +
     "tick spread + ~1 tick stop slippage ≈ 1.00 index point ≈ $2.00 per " +
     "contract round turn.")
costOvn = input.float(1.75, "Round-turn cost, overnight (index points)",
     minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = G_COST, tooltip = "Wider spread and a " +
     "thinner book outside 09:30-16:00 ET. Charging the RTH number around the " +
     "clock is the quiet way to invent an edge.")

G_UI = "Display"
showZones = input.bool(true, "Draw entry / stop / target", group = G_UI)
maxDraw = input.int(40, "Max trades drawn", minval = 1, maxval = 160, group = G_UI,
     tooltip = "Older drawings are deleted rather than left to be evicted.")
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group = G_UI)
dashPos = input.string("Top right", "Dashboard position", options =
     ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left"], group = G_UI)
colLong = input.color(#26a69a, "Win / long", group = G_UI)
colStop = input.color(#ef5350, "Loss / stop", group = G_UI)
colTgt = input.color(#42a5f5, "Target", group = G_UI)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Preset resolution — measured rows from backtest/improve.py, one position at a
// time, costs charged. PRESET_TABLE
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Measured on 519,046 5-minute bars, 2019-01-02 to 2026-08-10, one position at
// a time, costs charged by session. Reproduce with backtest/improve.py.
//
//   preset             WR      PF    trades/yr   net R   maxDD   alpha t
//   Balanced         43.8%   1.45      129      +247.5R   15.2R   +4.63
//   Max profit factor 28.5%  1.64      134      +292.1R   15.3R   +5.97
//   Max win rate     58.0%   1.29      170      +155.4R   14.6R   +2.54
//   Max trades       41.2%   1.17      414      +210.6R   25.7R   +2.96
//   (v1 for scale)   48.3%   1.18      319      +220.4R   19.4R   +2.82
//
// "alpha t" is the excess over random entries drawn from bars that already pass
// every gate except the breakout itself. The selection-corrected bar for this
// study's ~1,500 tested cells is t = 3.82. Balanced and Max profit factor clear
// it; Max win rate and Max trades do not, and are offered as preferences rather
// than as proven edges.
//
// All four share the same entry: 12-bar breakout, at least 1.5 ATR from the
// ET-day VWAP, outside the prior ET day's range, above the ~50-day EMA. They
// differ only in session, stop, target, time stop and breakeven.
isCustom = preset == "Custom"
isBal = preset == "Balanced"
isPf = preset == "Max profit factor"
isWr = preset == "Max win rate"
isTr = preset == "Max trades"

// Shared across every preset.
lookback     = isCustom ? lookbackIn     : 12
volRankMin   = isCustom ? volRankMinIn   : 0.0     // see note below
vwapMin      = isCustom ? vwapMinIn      : 1.5
usePd        = isCustom ? usePdIn        : true
closePosMin  = isCustom ? closePosMinIn  : 0.0
relVolMin    = isCustom ? relVolMinIn    : 0.0
marginAtr    = isCustom ? marginAtrIn    : 0.0
regimeSel    = isCustom ? regimeIn       : "Above EMA3900"
trailAtr     = isCustom ? trailIn        : 0.0
useFlat      = isCustom ? useFlatIn      : false
flatBy       = isCustom ? flatByIn       : 960

// The ATR-percentile gate that named this indicator is OFF in every preset, and
// that is a result rather than an oversight. Once entries are confined to the
// 09:30-13:00 window and to bars above the 50-day trend, the volatility filter
// is redundant: thresholds of 0.00 / 0.33 / 0.50 / 0.66 all score PF 1.65-1.67
// in-sample and 1.24-1.26 out-of-sample. Leaving it off keeps ~12% more trades
// for no measurable loss. Only 0.80 clearly hurts (PF 1.38). It stays exposed
// in Custom for anyone who wants it back.

// Per preset.
sessSel = isCustom ? sessIn : isTr ? "All hours" : "RTH morning"
stopMult = isCustom ? stopAtrIn : isWr ? 2.5 : isTr ? 3.5 : 2.0
rrMult = isCustom ? rrIn : isWr ? 1.0 : isTr ? 2.5 : 3.0
maxHold = isCustom ? maxHoldIn : isPf ? 144 : isWr ? 72 : 48
beR = isCustom ? beIn : (isPf or isTr) ? 0.75 : 0.0
expectTxt = isBal ? "PF 1.45 · WR 44% · 129/yr" :
     isPf ? "PF 1.64 · WR 29% · 134/yr" :
     isWr ? "PF 1.29 · WR 58% · 170/yr" :
     isTr ? "PF 1.17 · WR 41% · 414/yr" : "custom — no study row"

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ET clock. Every session and anchor decision below uses New York wall time, to
// match the research set exactly.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
etHour = hour(time, "America/New_York")
etMinute = minute(time, "America/New_York")
etMin = etHour * 60 + etMinute
etDay = dayofmonth(time, "America/New_York")
newEtDay = ta.change(etDay) != 0
tfMin = math.max(math.round(timeframe.in_seconds() / 60.0), 1)

RTH_OPEN = 570      // 09:30 ET
RTH_CLOSE = 960     // 16:00 ET
inRth = etMin >= RTH_OPEN and etMin < RTH_CLOSE

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ET-calendar-day VWAP. NOT ta.vwap() — see the header. Volume of zero (some
// index feeds) falls back to 1 per bar, which is what the research does, making
// this a plain typical-price average on those symbols rather than NaN.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var float cumPV = 0.0
var float cumVol = 0.0
barVol = nz(volume, 0.0) <= 0.0 ? 1.0 : volume
if newEtDay
    cumPV := 0.0
    cumVol := 0.0
cumPV := cumPV + hlc3 * barVol
cumVol := cumVol + barVol
vwapVal = cumVol > 0.0 ? cumPV / cumVol : hlc3

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Prior ET-calendar-day high/low, accumulated from chart bars. NOT
// request.security(..., "D", ...) — see the header.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var float dayHi = na
var float dayLo = na
var float pdHigh = na
var float pdLow = na
if newEtDay
    pdHigh := dayHi
    pdLow := dayLo
    dayHi := high
    dayLo := low
else
    dayHi := na(dayHi) ? high : math.max(dayHi, high)
    dayLo := na(dayLo) ? low : math.min(dayLo, low)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Indicators — all causal, all computed unconditionally so the series stay
// consistent (a ta.* call inside a branch is a classic Pine trap).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
atrVal = ta.atr(atrLen)
priorHigh = ta.highest(high, lookback)[1]     // extreme of the PREVIOUS N bars
atrRank = ta.percentrank(atrVal, volRankLen)  // 0.08% gate disagreement vs research
vwapDev = atrVal > 0 ? math.abs(close - vwapVal) / atrVal : 0.0
relVol = ta.sma(volume, 20) > 0 ? volume / ta.sma(volume, 20) : 1.0
barRange = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
closePos = (close - low) / barRange
ema200 = ta.ema(close, 200)
ema780 = ta.ema(close, 780)
ema1560 = ta.ema(close, 1560)
ema3900 = ta.ema(close, 3900)
var float pdClose = na
var float dayClose = na
if newEtDay
    pdClose := dayClose
dayClose := close

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Entry gates
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
passSess = sessSel == "All hours" ? true :
     sessSel == "RTH 09:30-16:00" ? inRth :
     sessSel == "RTH minus last 30m" ? (etMin >= RTH_OPEN and etMin < RTH_CLOSE - 30) :
     sessSel == "RTH morning" ? (etMin >= RTH_OPEN and etMin < 780) :
     sessSel == "07:00-16:00" ? (etMin >= 420 and etMin < RTH_CLOSE) :
     (etMin >= 180 and etMin < RTH_CLOSE)

passRegime = regimeSel == "None" ? true :
     regimeSel == "Above prior-day close" ? (not na(pdClose) and close > pdClose) :
     regimeSel == "Above EMA200" ? close > ema200 :
     regimeSel == "Above EMA780" ? close > ema780 :
     regimeSel == "Above EMA1560" ? close > ema1560 :
     close > ema3900

warm = bar_index > math.max(volRankLen, lookback) + atrLen and not na(atrVal) and
     atrVal > 0 and not na(priorHigh)
passVol = volRankMin <= 0 or atrRank > volRankMin
passVwap = vwapMin <= 0 or vwapDev >= vwapMin
passPd = not usePd or (not na(pdHigh) and not na(pdLow) and
     (close > pdHigh or close < pdLow))
passClosePos = closePosMin <= 0 or closePos >= closePosMin
passRelVol = relVolMin <= 0 or relVol >= relVolMin
breakout = close > priorHigh + marginAtr * atrVal
// Never open a position on the bar the flat-by rule would immediately close:
// that trade lasts zero bars and books nothing but the round turn.
flatBarNow = useFlat and ((etMin < flatBy and etMin + tfMin >= flatBy) or
     etMin + tfMin >= 1440)
passFlatEntry = not useFlat or etMin + tfMin < flatBy

longSignal = warm and barstate.isconfirmed and breakout and passVol and
     passVwap and passPd and passClosePos and passRelVol and passSess and
     passRegime and passFlatEntry

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Position state — strictly one trade at a time.
//
// Not cosmetic. Allowing overlapping entries inflates the trade count ~3.4x and
// profit factor from 1.19 to 1.33, because the same move gets counted several
// times over. One position at a time is what the reported statistics describe
// and what an account can actually hold.
//
// Evaluation order mirrors the research kernel exactly: manage the open
// position first (stop before target, so a bar spanning both books the stop),
// then consider a new entry. backtest/pine_parity.py asserts this file and the
// research engine produce identical trade lists.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var bool inTrade = false
var float entryPx = na
var float stopPx = na
var float tgtPx = na
var float riskPts = na
var float atrAtEntry = na
var float costR = 0.0
var int entryBar = na

var int nWin = 0
var int nLoss = 0
var int nProfit = 0        // any trade closed above breakeven, however it exited
var int nScratch = 0
var int nTimeout = 0
var int nFlat = 0
var float grossProfitR = 0.0
var float grossLossR = 0.0
var float netR = 0.0
var float peakR = 0.0
var float maxDdR = 0.0
var int nRth = 0
var float costPaidR = 0.0

var line lnEntry = na
var line lnStop = na
var line lnTgt = na
var array<line> drawn = array.new<line>()

enteredThisBar = false
closedThisBar = false
lastR = 0.0

// --- manage an open position -------------------------------------------------
// Pine functions cannot assign to globals, so the booking arithmetic is inlined.
if inTrade
    rBooked = 0.0
    didClose = false
    if low <= stopPx
        // Pessimistic: a bar spanning both levels books the stop. OHLC bars
        // hide the intrabar path, so ambiguity resolves against the strategy.
        rBooked := (stopPx - entryPx) / riskPts - costR
        if stopPx >= entryPx
            nScratch := nScratch + 1
        else
            nLoss := nLoss + 1
        didClose := true
    else if high >= tgtPx
        rBooked := rrMult - costR
        nWin := nWin + 1
        didClose := true
    else if bar_index - entryBar >= maxHold
        rBooked := (close - entryPx) / riskPts - costR
        nTimeout := nTimeout + 1
        didClose := true
    else if flatBarNow
        rBooked := (close - entryPx) / riskPts - costR
        nFlat := nFlat + 1
        didClose := true

    if didClose
        netR := netR + rBooked
        costPaidR := costPaidR + costR
        if rBooked > 0
            grossProfitR := grossProfitR + rBooked
            nProfit := nProfit + 1
        else
            grossLossR := grossLossR - rBooked
        inTrade := false
        closedThisBar := true
        lastR := rBooked
        if showZones and not na(lnEntry)
            line.set_xy2(lnEntry, bar_index, entryPx)
            line.set_xy2(lnStop, bar_index, stopPx)
            line.set_xy2(lnTgt, bar_index, tgtPx)
            col = rBooked > 0 ? colLong : colStop
            line.set_color(lnEntry, col)
    else
        // Stop moves are decided on the bar CLOSE — a stop cannot be moved on
        // information from inside a bar that has not printed yet — while stop
        // and target HITS are evaluated on the bar's high/low.
        if beR > 0 and close >= entryPx + beR * riskPts and stopPx < entryPx
            stopPx := entryPx
        if trailAtr > 0
            cand = close - trailAtr * atrAtEntry
            if cand > stopPx
                stopPx := cand
        if showZones and not na(lnEntry)
            line.set_xy2(lnEntry, bar_index, entryPx)
            line.set_xy2(lnStop, bar_index, stopPx)
            line.set_xy2(lnTgt, bar_index, tgtPx)

// --- open a new position -----------------------------------------------------
if longSignal and not inTrade
    riskCand = stopMult * atrVal
    if riskCand > 0
        inTrade := true
        enteredThisBar := true
        entryPx := close
        riskPts := riskCand
        atrAtEntry := atrVal
        stopPx := entryPx - riskPts
        tgtPx := entryPx + rrMult * riskPts
        entryBar := bar_index
        costR := (inRth ? costRth : costOvn) / riskPts
        nRth := nRth + (inRth ? 1 : 0)
        if showZones
            lnEntry := line.new(bar_index, entryPx, bar_index, entryPx,
                 color = colLong, width = 2)
            lnStop := line.new(bar_index, stopPx, bar_index, stopPx,
                 color = colStop, style = line.style_dashed)
            lnTgt := line.new(bar_index, tgtPx, bar_index, tgtPx,
                 color = colTgt, style = line.style_dashed)
            array.push(drawn, lnEntry)
            array.push(drawn, lnStop)
            array.push(drawn, lnTgt)
            // Delete our own oldest drawings instead of letting TradingView
            // evict them: eviction leaves the var references pointing at dead
            // ids, which is how v1 ended up silently dropping zones.
            while array.size(drawn) > maxDraw * 3
                line.delete(array.shift(drawn))

peakR := math.max(peakR, netR)
maxDdR := math.max(maxDdR, peakR - netR)

plotshape(enteredThisBar, title = "Long entry", style = shape.triangleup,
     location = location.belowbar, color = colLong, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(closedThisBar and lastR > 0, title = "Exit +", style = shape.xcross,
     location = location.abovebar, color = colLong, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(closedThisBar and lastR <= 0, title = "Exit -", style = shape.xcross,
     location = location.abovebar, color = colStop, size = size.tiny)

plot(showZones and inTrade ? stopPx : na, "Active stop", color = colStop,
     style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(showZones and inTrade ? tgtPx : na, "Active target", color = colTgt,
     style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Dashboard — grades this symbol's own history, costs charged, one at a time
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tblPos = dashPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right :
     dashPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left :
     dashPos == "Bottom right" ? position.bottom_right : position.bottom_left

var table dash = table.new(tblPos, 2, 14, border_width = 1,
     frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 60), frame_width = 1)

put(r, k, v, kc, vc) =>
    table.cell(dash, 0, r, k, text_size = size.small, text_color = kc,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, r, v, text_size = size.small, text_color = vc,
         text_halign = text.align_right)

if showDash and barstate.islast
    closed = nWin + nLoss + nScratch + nTimeout + nFlat
    // Win rate = trades that actually made money. Counting only target hits
    // against stop hits (and dropping scratches and time exits) reports ~18%
    // for a genuinely profitable configuration, which is just misleading.
    wr = closed > 0 ? 100.0 * nProfit / closed : 0.0
    pf = grossLossR > 0 ? grossProfitR / grossLossR : 0.0
    expR = closed > 0 ? netR / closed : 0.0
    avgCost = closed > 0 ? costPaidR / closed : 0.0
    tfSec = timeframe.in_seconds()
    tfOk = tfSec >= 180 and tfSec <= 900
    // The ET-day anchors need overnight bars to be correct. An RTH-only chart
    // silently redefines "prior-day range" and VWAP.
    hasOvernight = nRth < closed
    pfCol = pf >= 1.2 ? color.new(#26a69a, 0) :
         pf >= 1.0 ? color.new(#ffb74d, 0) : color.new(#ef5350, 0)
    kc = color.new(color.gray, 20)
    vc = color.new(color.gray, 10)
    good = color.new(#26a69a, 0)
    bad = color.new(#ef5350, 0)
    warn = color.new(#ffb74d, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "MMT Expansion Breakout v2", text_size = size.small,
         text_color = color.new(color.gray, 0), text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, preset, text_size = size.small,
         text_color = color.new(color.gray, 0), text_halign = text.align_right)

    put(1, "Trades graded", str.tostring(closed), kc, vc)
    put(2, "Win rate (profitable)", str.tostring(wr, "#.#") + "%", kc, vc)
    put(3, "Profit factor", str.tostring(pf, "#.##"), kc, pfCol)
    put(4, "Net R", str.tostring(netR, "+#.#;-#.#"), kc, netR > 0 ? good : bad)
    put(5, "Expectancy / trade", str.tostring(expR, "+#.###;-#.###"), kc,
         expR > 0 ? good : bad)
    put(6, "Max drawdown", str.tostring(maxDdR, "#.#") + "R", kc, vc)
    put(7, "Tgt / stop / BE / time / flat",
         str.tostring(nWin) + " / " + str.tostring(nLoss) + " / " +
         str.tostring(nScratch) + " / " + str.tostring(nTimeout) + " / " +
         str.tostring(nFlat), kc, vc)
    put(8, "Avg cost charged", str.tostring(100 * avgCost, "#.#") + "% of R", kc,
         color.new(color.gray, 30))
    put(9, "Open / session", (inTrade ? "in trade" : "flat") + " · " + sessSel, kc,
         color.new(color.gray, 30))
    put(10, "Management", (beR > 0 ? "BE@" + str.tostring(beR, "#.##") + "R" : "no BE") +
         " · " + (trailAtr > 0 ? "trail " + str.tostring(trailAtr, "#.#") + "atr" : "no trail"),
         kc, color.new(color.gray, 30))
    put(11, "Study expectation", expectTxt, kc, color.new(color.gray, 40))
    put(12, tfOk ? "Timeframe" : "⚠ Timeframe",
         tfOk ? timeframe.period : timeframe.period + " (built for 5m)", kc,
         tfOk ? color.new(color.gray, 30) : warn)
    put(13, hasOvernight ? "Chart session" : "⚠ Chart session",
         hasOvernight ? "includes overnight" : "RTH only — use ETH",
         kc, hasOvernight ? color.new(color.gray, 30) : warn)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Alerts
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(longSignal, "Expansion breakout long",
     "MMT: long breakout — expansion regime confirmed")

if enteredThisBar
    alert("MMT ExpBrk2 LONG @ " + str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick) +
         "  stop " + str.tostring(stopPx, format.mintick) +
         "  target " + str.tostring(tgtPx, format.mintick),
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if closedThisBar
    alert("MMT ExpBrk2 EXIT @ " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) +
         "  booked " + str.tostring(lastR, "+#.##;-#.##") + "R",
         alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
